  "theorem": "Over complex roots of unity, x+y=z+1 has no X60-filtered solutions: if z != -1, the midpoint of the chord {x,y} equals the midpoint of {z,1}, and a circle chord is determined by its midpoint; if z=-1 then y=-x.  Therefore every finite-field filtered solution gives a four-term word f=X^a+X^b-X^c-1 with f(zeta)=0 but Phi_n not dividing f over Z.  By the X30 norm-gate principle, p divides Res(Phi_n,f)."
